/*
Simple intuition

To reach step i, you can only come from:

step i-1 (take 1 step)

step i-2 (take 2 steps)

So the number of ways to reach step i is the sum of ways to reach the previous two steps.

This keeps building up until step n.
Time Complexity

O(n)
We compute each dp[i] once.

Space Complexity

O(n)
The DP array stores results for all steps.
*/
class Solution {
    public int climbStairs(int n) {
        if(n<=2)return n;
        int[] dp = new int[n+1];
        dp[1]=1;
        dp[2]=2;
        for(int i=3;i<=n;i++){
            dp[i]=dp[i-1]+dp[i-2];
        }
        return dp[n];
    }
}
